package Libraries.Language.Compile.Test

use Libraries.Testing.QuorumTest
use Libraries.Testing.ScriptCheck

/*
    How and/or are worked out when they're grouped inside each other, on
    variables (Expressions' BoolParens uses the literals true and false, one
    level deep). On 2026-11-23 the bytecode back end was found to get some
    groupings wrong: an and/or whose left side is a grouped and/or with
    another grouped and/or on its own right, such as
    (a or (b and c)) and d, can come out true when it should be false
    (Plans/Compiler/AndOrShortCircuitBug.md). These scripts try every
    grouping of two, three and four operators on every combination of
    true and false, as a value and as an if condition, and the shapes
    around the bug in the other places a condition can be, with calls
    that log which parts are worked out. More scripts widen it: chains
    without parentheses (and before or, left to right), not around groups,
    comparisons as the parts, 200 deeper expressions of five to eight
    operators, the exact order of calls for every grouping of three and
    four operators, and guards whose right side would fail if it ran
    (Guards, written by hand). The expected output is the
    correct answer, worked out separately, so these fail until the
    compiler is fixed. JavaScript and Python write the operators
    themselves (&& and ||, and and or), so they should pass there; they're
    run everywhere so a change to any back end is caught.
*/
class ShortCircuitTester
    QuorumTest suite = undefined
    ScriptCheck scripts
    text path = "Scripts/ShortCircuit/Pass/"

    action Test
        scripts:SetSuite(suite)
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "AllGroupingsTwo")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "AllGroupingsThree")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "AllGroupingsFour")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "Contexts")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "NoParentheses")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "NotGroupingsOne")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "NotGroupingsTwo")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "Comparisons")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "DeepGroupings")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "CallOrderThree")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "CallOrderFour")
        scripts:CheckEverywhere(path + "Guards")
    end

    action GetName returns text
        return "Short circuit Tests"
    end

    action GetCompilerTestSuite returns QuorumTest
        return suite
    end

    action SetCompilerTestSuite(QuorumTest suite)
        me:suite = suite
    end
end
